{"caption":"A close-up, dim view shows an oil lantern's burner assembly inside a glass globe. A bright yellow-orange flame with a faint blue base burns steadily at the center, its shape shifting slightly from frame to frame. A perforated metal ring surrounds the central wick holder, and a thin dark wire crosses the foreground diagonally. The flame remains lit, tilting and narrowing as the viewpoint changes.

As the excerpt continues, the framing widens and drops revealing more of the lantern's curved lower metal body. The perforated ring and burner remain roughly centered, but the diagonal wire shifts position across the flame because of the changing angle. A fingertip enters at the lower-left edge and stays near the dark base without visible adjustment. The flame's bright core and pale blue base persist while its outline leans and flickers.

The lantern body stays mostly stationary, with the apparent motion coming from the viewpoint's slow downward pull-back. The flame still burns inside the glass globe, the wire still crosses it, and a hand remains near the lantern base.","length_note":""}
